NEWS
====

This file summarizes user-visible changes to hostnamed, most recent first.
See ChangeLog.md for the complete release history.

0.3.1 (2026-10-21)
------------------
* Updated release metadata and man-page version strings for 0.3.1.
* Corrected the packaged release-history reference to ChangeLog.md.

0.3.0 (2026-10-16)
------------------
* Hostname and machine-info updates from hostnamectl use the system D-Bus
  API. The daemon performs privileged writes and polkit authorization.
* set-hostname preserves PRETTY_HOSTNAME unless a pretty-hostname change is
  explicitly requested.
* Atomic machine-info updates preserve unrelated keys, serialize cooperating
  writers with an advisory lock, and install the replacement file with mode
  0644.
* UUID parsing requires canonical 36-character UUID syntax and rejects
  all-zero and all-0xFF placeholder values.
* Hardware identification skips common DMI placeholder strings and uses
  device-tree data as a fallback where available.
* Improved regression checks for privileged writes, authorization wiring,
  UUID validation, file modes, packaging, and hostnamectl's D-Bus usage.
* polkit is a required build dependency; the obsolete -Dpolkit option has
  been removed.

0.2.6 (2026-06-20)
------------------
* Polkit checks became asynchronous so authentication prompts do not block
  the daemon's main loop.
* GetProductUUID and GetHardwareSerial gained dedicated polkit actions.
* Fixed a polkit authorization bypass and a D-Bus JSON-escaping bug.
* Machine-info values are validated in the writer as defence in depth.

0.2.0 (2026-06-19)
------------------
* Added configurable os-release and machine-info paths.
* Improved pretty-hostname derivation from FQDN input.
* FirmwareDate is exposed as a D-Bus uint64 in microseconds since the Unix
  epoch.
* Machine-info property-cache updates emit PropertiesChanged directly.

0.1.0 (2026-05-31 - 2026-06-17)
--------------------------------
* First public implementation of org.freedesktop.hostname1 over plain D-Bus,
  without a systemd/logind dependency.
* Implemented hostname and machine-info setters gated by polkit.
* Added validation for hostnames and machine-info values.
* Added hostnamectl and localectl companion scripts and SlackBuild packaging.

BUGS
====

Known issues and areas that still need target-system verification for 0.3.1.
These items are not necessarily release blockers. Please report issues at
https://github.com/nater1983/hostnamed/issues

* End-to-end authorization should be verified on the target distribution with
  both an authorized wheel user and an unauthorized unprivileged user. The
  regression tests inspect authorization wiring but do not replace testing
  with the real system bus, polkit daemon, and an authentication agent.
* Interactive authorization depends on a working polkit authentication agent
  in the caller's desktop session. Headless sessions may be unable to complete
  an interactive challenge.
* Recovery after the system D-Bus daemon restarts has not been fully validated
  end-to-end; test name loss and re-acquisition with the target service setup.
* External edits to watched files are detected through inotify. Very rapid
  successive writes may be coalesced, and behavior under heavy inotify queue
  load has not been stress-tested.
* The DMI placeholder list is finite; unknown firmware template strings may
  still be reported. Device-tree HardwareVendor uses the vendor prefix from
  the first compatible entry rather than a marketing name, and some boards do
  not provide a chassis-type property.
* Virtualization is not inferred as "vm" or "container". Chassis is derived
  from machine-info, SMBIOS, and device-tree data.
* machine-info parsing supports double-quoted values and currently uses the
  first matching key if duplicate keys exist.
* Slackware startup behavior for fully qualified values in /etc/HOSTNAME should
  be verified against the target system's rc.S; hostnamed passes the configured
  static hostname to sethostname().
* Translation loading by the daemon has not been verified on installed systems;
  confirm that translations under the configured locale directory are found.
